  "title": "Access is local: a plane piece keeps it whatever happens elsewhere",
  "subject": "Whether access at a gluing line depends only on the planar piece around that line",
  "conclusion": "Plane signed systems with as many lines as odd faces have perfect matchings as solutions and the access lemma for every pinning, and in a splice an intact side acts on the cut as the point or line it replaced. So every pinning by two points of a plane piece has access wherever the removal is, and only pinnings from inside an opened handle can fail.",
